# oracle: pair_style body/rounded/polyhedron with friction mu 0.5 and the keyword history (tangential spring per pair, k_t 2/7 k_n): the two rounded cubes of w121body_cubes_friction (approach at speed 2, a lateral sliding velocity, one cube turned 30 degrees about z, the other offset in y), fix nve/body, 2000 steps: thermo pe ke etotal press and the atom state
# Measured (engine vs native, max relative error): below 1e-13 (passes at rel 1e-13 abs 1e-12, measured by tightening the tolerance). The native run with the history keyword differs from the run without it, so the history term is exercised.
# oracle-inputs: w121body_cubes_friction.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-12
units           lj
dimension       3
atom_style      body rounded/polyhedron 1 8
atom_modify     map array
read_data       w121body_cubes_friction.data
set             atom 1 vx 2.0 vy 0.5 vz 0.0
set             atom 2 vx -2.0 vy 0.0 vz 0.0
pair_style      body/rounded/polyhedron 20 5 0.5 1 0.5 history
pair_coeff      * * 100 1
comm_modify     vel yes
neighbor        0.5 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
timestep        0.001
fix             1 all nve/body
group           g1 id 1
compute         t1 all property/atom tqx tqy tqz angmomx angmomy angmomz
compute         r1 g1 reduce sum c_t1[1] c_t1[2] c_t1[3] c_t1[4] c_t1[5] c_t1[6]
thermo_style    custom step pe ke etotal press c_r1[1] c_r1[2] c_r1[3] c_r1[4] c_r1[5] c_r1[6]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          50
run             2000
